Chapter: Fat32Longwrite

  cites Foreword chapter Fat32
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 FAT32 gained a long-name READER on 2026-09-01 and could still only WRITE an
 8.3 entry, so every name this library wrote came back under its alias and a
 caller that wrote `LongNameOnFat32.txt` could not read it by that name.
 `codex/test/fat32-longname` grades the reader against runs laid down by
 hand, deliberately, because a reader graded by our own encoder would agree
 with itself whatever both did. This chapter is the other half and it has the
 opposite obligation: the writer is graded by the reader, so every arm here
 is a round trip and the discriminating ones are the two that would still
 pass if the run were never written.

 Arm B is the one that pays. Two names share the first six characters, so
 they are offered the same alias, and only a search of the DIRECTORY can tell
 them apart. Their contents differ, so reading each long name and getting the
 other one's bytes is a failure the arm can express. A writer that skipped
 the search would give both `LONGNA~1.TXT` and one of the two reads would
 answer the wrong file rather than answering nothing.

 Arm A's second read is the control in the other direction: a long-named file
 must STILL answer under its 8.3 alias, because the short entry is what every
 8.3 reader sees and the run is an addition to it, not a replacement.

 We say:

Section: Reporting

  f32w-say : Maybe Text -> Text
  f32w-say (m) = when m
    is Just (t) -> t
    is None -> "<none>"

  f32w-rep : Integer, Text -> Text
  f32w-rep (n) (acc) =
    if n <= 0 then acc
    else f32w-rep (n - 1) (acc & "N")

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  opening = act
    fmt <- fat32-format 2048 30720 "CODEX"
    print-line-uni ("format " & show fmt)

    vol <- fat32-init 2048
    print-line-uni ("root cluster " & show (vol.f32-root-cluster)
      & " spc " & show (vol.f32-sectors-per-cluster))

    print-line-uni ("A slots " & show (fat32-slots-for "LongNameOnFat32.txt"))

    a <- fat32-write-file vol "LongNameOnFat32.txt" [72, 105]
    print-line-uni ("A write " & show a)

    a1 <- fat32-read-text vol "LongNameOnFat32.txt"
    print-line-uni ("A by long name " & f32w-say a1)

    a2 <- fat32-read-text vol "LONGNA~1.TXT"
    print-line-uni ("A by alias " & f32w-say a2)

    a3 <- fat32-read-text vol "LongNameOnFat32"
    print-line-uni ("A no truncated ghost " & f32w-say a3)

    b <- fat32-write-file vol "LongNameOnFat32-second.txt" [79, 75]
    print-line-uni ("B write " & show b)

    b1 <- fat32-read-text vol "LongNameOnFat32-second.txt"
    print-line-uni ("B by long name " & f32w-say b1)

    b2 <- fat32-read-text vol "LONGNA~2.TXT"
    print-line-uni ("B by second alias " & f32w-say b2)

    b3 <- fat32-read-text vol "LongNameOnFat32.txt"
    print-line-uni ("A survives B " & f32w-say b3)

    c <- fat32-write-file vol "SHORT.TXT" [90]
    print-line-uni ("C write " & show c
      & " slots " & show (fat32-slots-for "SHORT.TXT"))

    c1 <- fat32-read-text vol "SHORT.TXT"
    print-line-uni ("C by its own name " & f32w-say c1)

    d <- fat32-write-file vol "LongDirectoryName/inner.txt" [68, 111, 116]
    print-line-uni ("D write " & show d)

    d1 <- fat32-read-text vol "LongDirectoryName/inner.txt"
    print-line-uni ("D through a long directory " & f32w-say d1)

    let over = f32w-rep 300 ""
    in act
      e <- fat32-write-file vol (over & ".txt") [1]
      print-line-uni ("E past 255 refused " & show (e == False))

      e1 <- fat32-read-text vol "LongNameOnFat32.txt"
      print-line-uni ("A survives the refusal " & f32w-say e1)
    end
  end

